index c9ee424..4dc6318 100644
--- a/specs/hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md
+++ b/specs/hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md
@@ -68,3 +68,10 @@ Resume gets a client back into one conversation: the id it names, or the user's
 ## When the store cannot answer
 
 - A store whose collection fails rejects rather than answering a partial or empty list: what to show a user who may have conversations is the caller's decision, and an empty history is not a safe guess ([validated by: rejects rather than answering a partial list when the collection fails](../../src/infrastructure/stores/mongo/mongoConversationList.test.ts#L225)).
+
+## Over the WebSocket
+
+- The engine answers the list on the socket itself, so a consumer need not stand up a second authenticated route over the same personal data: `list_conversations` is answered with one `conversation_list` of the connecting user's own summaries, newest first (see [the WebSocket protocol spec](../hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md), § 4.3 and § 5.9) ([validated by: answers the connecting user with their own newest-first list, however the frame names its owner](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L230)).
+- The user id is taken from the connection and never from the frame, and a row carries no conversation content, so the socket discloses exactly what `listFor` does and nothing more ([validated by: answers the connecting user with their own newest-first list, however the frame names its owner](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L230)).
+- Making that disclosure is the deployer's decision, not the client's: with `transport.history` off, and whenever the store cannot list, the frame is answered with an error rather than an empty history ([validated by: answers with an error, not an empty list, whenever the list cannot be served](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L293)).
+- Opening a conversation from the list needs no new transport code: an id from a row, sent back as `?sessionId=<id>`, is rejoined with `resumed: true` and its replay by the resume that already checks ownership ([validated by: hands a row from the list to the resume that already exists, end to end](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L391)).
